      "reasoning": {
        "hypothesis": "An authenticated user who can obtain the AddFormNotice nonce from a whitelisted admin screen can call the AJAX handler without a capability check, allowing them to globally dismiss the Add Form notice or retrieve a fixed redirect URL. Unlike the sibling ConnectionNotice handler, AddFormNotice::handle_ajax_action() performs no current_user_can() check.",
        "trace": "AddFormNotice::init() registers add_action('wp_ajax_hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_action', ...) at src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:28 \u2014 authenticated-only (wp_ajax_, not wp_ajax_nopriv_) \u2192 handle_ajax_action() at line 43 \u2192 check_ajax_referer(self::NOTICE_ACTION, 'nonce') at line 44 \u2192 no capability check \u2192 $choice from sanitize_text_field($_POST['choice']) \u2192 'dismiss' branch: set_transient(NOTICE_DISMISS_TRANSIENT, true, WEEK_IN_SECONDS) at line 59 and wp_send_json_success(); 'success' branch: wp_send_json_success(array('redirect_url' => 'admin.php?page=hostinger-reach&addForm=1')) at line 66",
        "conclusion": "REVIEW. The missing capability check is a real design inconsistency vs ConnectionNotice. However, exploitation requires an authenticated user to obtain the nonce from enqueue_notice_assets() \u2014 which only runs when should_render() is true, gated to specific admin screen IDs (dashboard, pages, posts, edit-page, edit-post). In default WordPress configurations, users with roles below editor/author cannot access these admin screens. The concrete impact is limited to: (a) globally dismissing the Add Form onboarding notice for one week, (b) returning a fixed admin redirect URL string. Neither affects credentials, user permissions, plugin configuration, or security settings. Retained as REVIEW because the design inconsistency is real, but escalation framing is removed \u2014 this is a notice management surface, not privilege escalation.",
        "defenses": [
          "wp_ajax_ hook (not wp_ajax_nopriv_) at src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:28: handler only reachable by authenticated users",
          "check_ajax_referer(self::NOTICE_ACTION, 'nonce') at line 44: requires a valid action-specific nonce",
          "should_render() at line 100: nonce is only enqueued via enqueue_notice_assets() when the admin screen ID matches the whitelist (dashboard, pages, posts, edit-page, edit-post) AND the site is connected AND forms have not been added AND the notice is not dismissed \u2014 restricts nonce distribution to users who can access those screens"
        ],
        "refutation": [
          "REFUTATION ATTEMPT: Can a subscriber-level user access the whitelisted admin screens to obtain the nonce? RESULT: Largely refuted in default WordPress. Subscribers can access their profile page (screen ID 'profile') but cannot access 'dashboard' (requires read capability) or 'pages'/'posts'/'edit-page'/'edit-post' (require edit_posts or edit_pages capabilities, which authors/editors have but subscribers do not). A subscriber-level attacker typically cannot obtain the nonce without an additional vulnerability.",
          "REFUTATION ATTEMPT: What is the concrete impact of dismissal if exploited? RESULT: Exploitation would dismiss the Add Form onboarding notice site-wide for one week (set_transient at line 59) or return the fixed string 'admin.php?page=hostinger-reach&addForm=1' (line 66). This has no effect on credentials, plugin security configuration, stored user data, or access control. Not privilege escalation."
        ],
        "why_uncertain": "Exploitation depends on whether any authenticated role below editor can access the whitelisted admin screens on the target installation. Default WordPress restricts these, but custom role configurations or additional plugins may change this.",
        "resolution_path": "Confirm whether any sub-editor role on a default WordPress installation can access admin screens matching screen IDs 'dashboard', 'pages', 'posts', 'edit-page', or 'edit-post' and thus receive the localized nonce at src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:155."
      },
      "poc_description": "Requires authenticated access to a whitelisted admin screen (dashboard, pages, posts, edit-page, or edit-post). 1. Log in with a role that can access one of those screens. 2. Navigate to the qualifying screen. 3. Extract the nonce from the hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_data JS object (action key: 'hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_action'). 4. POST to admin-ajax.php with action=hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_action&nonce=<value>&choice=dismiss. 5. Observe the Add Form notice is globally suppressed for one week.",
      "cvss_vector": null,
      "remediation": "Add current_user_can('manage_options') check to AddFormNotice::handle_ajax_action() immediately after check_ajax_referer(), mirroring the pattern in ConnectionNotice::handle_ajax_action().",
